There is no such as official CLL 1.2.
Even CLL 1.0 and CLL 1.1 can be named official only if LLG considers *.
lojban.org pages official but there was no procedure in making them
official. John Cowan wrote CLL 1.0, that's it. Robin Powell published CLL
1.1 with a bunch of fixes compared to CLL 1.0, that's it.

There is a list of errata in CLL, whichla mezohe and la gleki recently
turned into a table:

https://mw.lojban.org/papri/CLL,_aka_Reference_Grammar,_Errata

If you fork https://github.com/lojban/cll/ and then apply prs from
https://github.com/lojban/cll/milestone/12 there then you may get something
like CLL 1.2 (mostly fixes of mistypes in English sentences)


